       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults, and I don't see a reason for that dose in this patient's details. Going above 200 mg raises the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT effects, seizures, and GI and CNS adverse effects. The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg once daily.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **200 mg once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **50 mg once daily**, the usual starting dose for depression or anxiety. For PTSD or panic disorder, the starting dose is often 25 mg.\n- **Another dose.** If so, tell me the dose and the indication.\n\nIf 400 mg is intentional, for example a specialist-directed regimen for refractory illness, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's above the labeled maximum and that you've confirmed it. I'd also recommend checking with pharmacy or psychiatry first."
      }
